A Binary Search Tree (BST) is a type of Binary Tree data structure, where the 
following properties must be true for any node "X" in the tree:
➢The X node's left child and all its descendants (children, children's children, and so 
on) have lower values than X's value.
➢The right child, and all its descendants have higher values than X's value.
➢Left and right subtrees must also be Binary Search Trees.
These properties makes it faster to search, add and delete values than a regular 
binary tree.
