SEARCHING IN BINARY SEARCH TREE
Three steps of searching:
•The item which is to be searched is compared with the root node. 
➢If the item is equal to the root, then we are done.
➢If its less than the root node then we search in the left sub-tree.
➢If its more than the root node then we search in the right sub-tree.
The above process will continue till the item is found or you reached end 
of the tree.
